# Smart Calculator

Hi, I'm Haider Sultan, an Electrical Engineering student currently learning Python.

I built this Smart Calculator as one of my beginner Python projects. The main purpose of this project was to practice the Python fundamentals I've been learning and to understand how different concepts work together in a real program.

The calculator is simple, but it helped me practice writing functions, working with user input, using conditions and loops, and handling basic errors.

## What the Calculator Does

The calculator can perform several basic operations:

* Addition
* Subtraction
* Multiplication
* Division
* Modulus
* Power

The program also allows the user to perform multiple calculations without having to restart it every time.

## Python Concepts Used

While working on this project, I practiced:

* Variables
* User input
* Data types and type conversion
* If, elif, and else statements
* While loops
* Functions
* Arithmetic operators
* Try and except
* Basic error handling
* Formatted output

These are some of the main Python concepts I've been working on as I learn the language.

## How to Run the Project

This project does not require any external Python libraries.

First, make sure Python is installed on your computer.

You can check your Python version with:

```bash
python --version
```

Then download or clone this repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/python-fundamentals-portfolio.git
```

Go into the project folder:

```bash
cd python-fundamentals-portfolio
```

Then run the calculator:

```bash
python calculator.py
```

## Example

A typical calculation looks something like this:

```text
==============================
        SMART CALCULATOR
==============================

Enter first number: 25
Enter second number: 5

Choose an operation:
1. Addition
2. Subtraction
3. Multiplication
4. Division
5. Modulus
6. Power

Enter your choice: 1

Result: 30
```

